Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraFiberBundleQ", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"2a8b6593-b438-4b16-840d-4896281c9f95"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraFiberBundleQ"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFiberBundleQ", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["fib", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a3b2c205-a4ea-4810-a5fe-7d3a4fb8822b"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "tests whether ",
 StyleBox["fib", "TI"],
 " has a common fiber graph and an adjacency-preserving matching over every \
base edge.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"482eb4ba-2d6a-4777-adf4-f9c89e82be21"],

Cell["\<\
The fibers must be mutually isomorphic, including across disconnected base \
components.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8980b3fa-214f-4634-bf9f-d8fd9f558a18"],

Cell["\<\
Every total vertex has exactly one transverse neighbour over each adjacent \
base vertex. Each resulting fiber bijection preserves vertical adjacency.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ff91dbf-4f9c-4f31-af29-a87a8f7b91ef"],

Cell["\<\
This is the finite Cartesian graph-bundle condition. The inverse image of a \
base edge is a Cartesian product of that edge with the common fiber, \
respecting the projection.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1d5cce5f-0f67-42c1-9b3f-20b031d42695"],

Cell["\<\
No topology or higher-dimensional cells are supplied by the predicate.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9a26e7d2-041e-413f-bb48-687c9a29eb18"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Twisted coverings with a common sheet count are bundles. Trivial monodromy \
is a separate question, tested for a selected connection by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFlatConnectionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFlatConnectionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d60a9cbb-a4ce-4e33-bb97-31f58ee58132"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d850bd24-3b51-421d-a58f-f19096705805"],

Cell["\<\
A covering may have different sheet counts on disconnected base components; \
such a covering is not a bundle with one common fiber.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b2fd2b14-6f4b-4172-a5d1-cd796a0f1d95"],

Cell["\<\
A nonempty list is tested by conjunction. An empty list is False; the empty \
fibered graph is a bundle. Unsupported inputs remain unevaluated.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2a408d67-0386-49ad-b5ee-a904f680719a"]
}, Open  ]],

